-- VARIANT WITHOUT A DOT ---------------------------------------- main.kl  K0917

An enum variant is written with a leading `.`: `.Circle(r)`, not `Circle(r)`. The dot means "a variant of the type expected here".

6│     let s: Shape = Circle(radius: 1.0)
                      ^^^^^^

Try: `.`

Help: Add `.` before the variant name. `kalam fix` does this for you.

Learn more: kalam explain K0917
